  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 0.5,
      "text": "Rendering a sheet is not releasing it. The release step has a name you would not guess."
    },
    {
      "t": 4.8,
      "text": "Render the sheet with the waves locked together, and hold on to the id it prints."
    },
    {
      "t": 10.8,
      "text": "The obvious word for the next step is not the word. There is no such command."
    },
    {
      "t": 16.8,
      "text": "This is the one, and it takes that id we were given."
    },
    {
      "t": 22.8,
      "text": "And the status now names what has been released."
    },
    {
      "t": 28.8,
      "text": "Now suppose somebody tidies the file up afterwards."
    },
    {
      "t": 34.8,
      "text": "Releasing it again is refused. What was released no longer matches what is on disk."
    },
    {
      "t": 40.8,
      "text": "So we render it again, and it tells us the id of what is now on disk."
    },
    {
      "t": 46.8,
      "text": "Release that, and it goes through. Always release what is actually there."
    },
    {
      "t": 50.5,
      "text": "Release the id the render printed, and if the file is touched afterwards, render it again before releasing."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Teaches that the release step is latch rather than release, that it takes the id the render printed, and that it refuses once the file has changed."
}
